mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 6 item 4 (Horizon WSI backend)
Why: wsi_horizon_get_extent read NWindow::default_*, the BufferQueue's
 answer, and that is why patch 0040's dock path has never fired on
 hardware. 0040 wrote "VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR HAS NEVER BEEN RETURNED ON
 HARDWARE" and treated it as coverage nobody had managed to get. It was
 not coverage. The queue cannot report a display mode change, so
 currentExtent could never move, so wsi_horizon_extent_changed could
 never return true, and no swapchain could be suboptimal because of a
 dock.
 .
 Patch 0054 made that matter more rather than less: with the application
 choosing its own extent, a mode change is the ONLY thing left that can
 make a swapchain suboptimal.
Evidence: RUN ON A CONSOLE 2026-08-24, tests/t_dock.c, docking and
 undocking three times with a buffer queued every 50 ms so the
 consumer's answer was being refreshed throughout:
 .
   CHANGE 1 at 7201 ms: mode 0 -> 1, dimensions 1280x720 -> 1280x720,
     default_ 1280x720 -> 1280x720, DisplayResolution 1280x720 ->
     1280x720
   CHANGE 2 at 7554 ms: mode 1 -> 1, dimensions 1280x720 -> 1280x720,
     default_ 1280x720 -> 1280x720, DisplayResolution 1280x720 ->
     1920x1080
 .
 Three sources and they disagree. appletGetOperationMode() moves and
 AppletHookType_OnOperationMode fires, so a dock does reach the process.
 nwindowGetDimensions() and NWindow::default_* never move at all — the
 compositor scales this layer to the television rather than resizing it.
 appletGetDefaultDisplayResolution() follows to 1920x1080 and back, on
 every one of the three docks, about 350 ms behind the mode. That is the
 source this now reads.
 .
 UNDOCKED THE TWO AGREE, both 1280x720, which is why this is a small
 change and not a redesign — and it is checked rather than asserted.
 With it, on the same build: t_vk_suboptimal 273/273 twice, t_vk_wsi_mt
 71/71, t_vk_present_draw 183/183, t_vk_immediate 442/442,
 t_vk_swapchain 144/144, and the surface still publishes "current
 1280x720, min 16x16, max 1280x720" exactly as before.
 .
 NOT RUN: the docked half. Nothing in a process can resize a VI layer,
 so somebody has to dock the console during t_vk_swapchain's section G
 or t_vk_suboptimal's section D — which, for the first time, can now
 actually fire. docs/PENDING-VERIFICATION.md § 1.1 carries it, together
 with the second question that opens: the surface then reports 1920x1080
 while the layer stays 1280x720, so maxImageExtent allows a 1080p
 swapchain the compositor would scale down, and nothing has measured
 that either.
Upstream: no — the whole file is Horizon-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
